# trn1.2xlarge (us-east-1), 2026-09-10. What sets memory_read's rate?
# Raw output; host paths removed. Probe: variants of the memory_read kernel, 2 GiB bf16
# all-ones, 20 s each, each in its own process on core 0 (NEURON_RT_VISIBLE_CORES=0);
# engine profiles captured on core 1. _percent counters are 0-1 fractions.
#   A sum free 2048 (the shipped kernel)   B sum free 8192   E sum free 512
#   D sumsq free 2048 (cast + t*t + sum)   F/G sum as fp32 without an explicit cast
# PREDICTED: vector-bound -> D << A, B ~= A ~= E, vector ~1.0;
#            DMA-bound    -> D ~= A, vector well below 1.0.

